From e70603dba05ca77b8c817fc692ce2f67459086e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Kraus <406385+benkraus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:32:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Build srv-front on macOS

srv-front only exchanges JSON with backends, but it imported vmrunner for
the cold-disk migration message types, which pulled in the Firecracker
SDK and CNI, and its remaining dependencies used Linux-only syscalls.

- Move MigrationDisk, MigrationDiskRequest and MigrationDiskResult into
  internal/migrationdisk (Transfer, Request, Result) so srv-front no
  longer depends on vmrunner.
- host: read the kernel release with x/sys/unix.Uname, available on
  Linux and macOS.
- storage: compute available bytes independent of the statfs field
  width; keep the O_PATH opener in open_linux.go with an unsupported
  stub elsewhere.
- coldstore: route RENAME_NOREPLACE renames through renameNoReplace,
  Linux-only with an unsupported stub elsewhere.
- CI cross-builds srv-front for darwin/arm64 and darwin/amd64.
- Document running srv-front on macOS under launchd, with an example
  LaunchDaemon in contrib/launchd.

Linux behaviour is unchanged.
